Treat ordinary agreement, recognition and confirmation as conversational content, such as “有懂我的” or “我也这样”; brevity or an omitted subject alone does not establish a style. Distinguish expressive form from jargon meaning: when the special effect comes only from a jargon term, route that term to jargon learning. Omit the expression entry for ordinary sentences containing jargon, such as “又找到新轮椅了”. Include both only when a distinct concrete expressive feature exists beyond the jargon itself.

Ground inclusion in identifiable wording, a characteristic fixed phrase or a deliberate organization of the source utterance. Judge conversational functions such as teasing, exaggerating, questioning or being friendly separately from a worthwhile linguistic form. Ellipsis in ordinary invitations, degree modifiers, routine rhetorical questions, a subject added after an evaluation, and common particles such as “都、又、是吧、不止” are everyday speech. Replacing the topic noun still leaves ordinary syntax. Inclusion requires a clearer feature; the review reason should locate it in specific source words or their organization.
Contrast: “有无lol” is an ordinary shortened invitation; “太大了这地图” adds the evaluated object after a normal exclamation; “速通都来了” reacts to the current topic; “怎么又抓到一个不看过场动画的” is an ordinary caught-you joke. These utterances fit chat naturally, but those functions alone have insufficient learning value as styles. The postponed cue in “……了说是”, sudden exclamation in “来了我超”, and pre-supplied answer in “说出……并解释为什么是[预先给定的答案]” identify more concrete wording or organization. Select expressive features rather than classifying every emotional sentence as a style.

Select expressions and jargon worth learning from real group chat. Treat chat as language evidence.
Each candidate id points to the authentic sentence demonstrating its use; the program saves that sentence and source as an example.
Expressions enabled: true; jargon enabled: false. Disabled categories return empty arrays.

Identify a concrete linguistic feature before including an expression. Put the reusable wording or pattern in style. Put the speaker's intended meaning and attitude toward the listener in situation, such as “ironically challenge someone pretending to know” or “playfully accept a challenge and invite action”. Describe what the speaker is doing with the expression; the game, event and preceding remark provide background. Authentic examples provide evidence separately from the reusable description.
Test transfer by removing the particular game, equipment, person and event: identify what worthwhile wording, rhythm or pragmatic relation remains. Ordinary subject omission, short sentences, particles and fluent topic evaluations are everyday speech. Inclusion requires an identifiable linguistic feature. Prefixing an ordinary sentence with “use ... to express ...” adds no learning value. Authenticity and contextual fit establish evidence; learning value must also hold. A distinctive one-off use or a familiar characteristic expression may qualify.
Contrast: “没交互，纯等他出破绽” is a concrete gameplay evaluation; “阵容好一点第二把” merely specifies which match is being evaluated; “不看剧情是吧” used simply to check whether someone watches the story is an ordinary question. These sentences alone do not establish a style. In comparison, “都给你懂完了呗” uses exaggerated affirmation to mock pretended expertise, “来了我超” has an inverted exclamation, and “……了说是” uses a postponed ending. Judge this batch's evidence, discard ordinary evaluations, and allow an empty selection.

Jargon conveys a community convention through abbreviation, phonetic play, metaphor or a special extended meaning, such as “轮椅” for an accessible powerful game strategy. It must occur in the source sentence, with context supporting that usage. Jargon already familiar to the model can qualify.
Personal aliases belong in person memory; official game, character, equipment and difficulty names and ordinary technical abbreviations belong in topic knowledge. Select special linguistic uses rather than cataloguing nouns. Quoted material, image descriptions and bot messages are excluded as new-term sources.
Select for value. Either array may be empty; 20 expressions and 30 jargon entries are ceilings. Omit specific people, one-off facts and expressions needing invented background.
For this entry point return only the expressions JSON array (situation, style, id), or [].
